
CPG_SPE9.DATA: is the data file for SPE9 with a Corner Point Geometry 

TOPVALUES file is not necessary for CP geometry so it has been removed.

Changes implemeted from last spe9_new files:
- In keyword COMPDAT item 8 (transmissibility factors) must be entered to get a match between Eclipse and Flow runs. This is being corrected and default values are used.


- Last line of PVTO is calculated @ 4600 psi, not 5000psi, because the SPE paper specify a way to calculate Bo 1000psi over Psta which is 3600psi (during simulation, P does not exceed 3600 psi).

- The grid has been made on Excel.

SPE9.DATA (block-centred grid from DX, DY, DZ and TOPSVALUES.DATA) and SPE9_CP.DATA are the same
apart from the grid, so the results can be compared. Both grids have a dip of 10 degrees in the
x-direction with 300 ft horizontal block size, i.e. a depth step of 300*tan(10 deg) = 52.898 ft per
cell. (SPE9.GRDECL earlier used 300*sin(10 deg) = 52.094 ft, a dip of 9.85 degrees. The ECLIPSE
results in eclipse-simulation/ and the OPM reference results were made with that grid.)
